.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt REDUCO 1
.Os reduco VERSION
.Sh NAME
.Nm reduco
.Nd bring programs back after their world ended
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Fl p Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Fl x Ar name
.Nm
.Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
remembers how a program was started, notices whether it ended on purpose
or was killed together with its surroundings, and starts it again on request.
It does not depend on the host it runs under.
.Pp
Without a mode option,
.Nm
lists the records of this host, one per line, sorted by name, with tab
separated fields: state, name, info, working directory and command.
The state is
.Sq alive
when a guard holds the lock of the record, with the guard's process ID as
info, and
.Sq dead
otherwise, with the recorded cause of death as info, or
.Sq -
if there is none.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
as the record store.
.It Fl p Ar name
Print the record
.Ar name
as a
.Xr sh 1
command line that changes to the recorded directory and executes the recorded
command.
.It Fl x Ar name
Delete the record
.Ar name .
A record that is alive is refused.
.It Fl v
Print version information to standard output and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ev REDUCO_DIR
Record store, used when
.Fl d
is not given.
.It Ev HOME
The record store defaults to
.Pa $HOME/.reduco .
.El
.Sh FILES
Each record is a directory
.Pa name@host
in the record store, where
.Ar name
consists of letters, digits,
.Sq \&. ,
.Sq _
and
.Sq -
and does not start with
.Sq \&. .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa argv
The command, each argument terminated by a NUL byte.
.It Pa cwd
The working directory.
.It Pa died
The cause of death, if known.
.It Pa lock
Held with
.Xr fcntl 2
by the guard while the program runs.
.El
.Pp
The record store is created with mode 0700 and refused if it is not owned by
the caller or is writable by group or others.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr abduco 1 ,
.Xr dvtm 1
